# graphify — knowledge graph output, all of it regenerated from source by
# `graphify update .` (AST only, no API cost), so none of it is worth committing:
#   graph.json, graph.html   megabytes that churn on every code edit
#   cache/                   content-hashed extraction cache, machine-local
#   manifest.json            mtimes and hashes, differ on every machine
#   .graphify_python         absolute path to a local interpreter
#   GRAPH_REPORT.md, wiki/, obsidian/, cypher.txt, graph.svg, graph.graphml
#   <YYYY-MM-DD>/            per-run snapshot
# `.graphifyignore` IS committed — it is project configuration, not output.
# If the graph is ever wanted in version control, install graphify's union merge
# driver first (`graphify merge-driver`); without it graph.json conflicts on
# every branch.
/graphify-out/

# serena — LSP symbol cache and project configuration
/.serena/

# This is my automated changes directory, which is generated by my own scripts.
.changes/
artifacts/
company_tui.egg-info/
tools/

# tests/ was ignored here, which is why this repository had none: the definition of
# done asks for `python -m unittest discover` to pass and for focused tests under
# tests/, and nothing under an ignored path can be either. `test/` and `test.*` below
# still cover scratch files.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
dist/

test.*
test/

# Code signing. The private keys and the password never go in, the trust anchors always
# do - a committed .sha256 is the only thing that can tell a fetched certificate from a
# same-named different one, and `!` un-ignores it explicitly because git cannot un-ignore
# a file inside a directory that has been excluded wholesale.
certs/
*.pfx
*.p12
.dti_configs/signing.env
.dti_configs/logs/
!.dti_configs/*.sha256
!.dti_configs/share.env
